      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find \\(\\cos 135^\\circ\\), we can use the unit circle and the properties of trigonometric functions.\n\n1. **Identify the reference angle:**\n   The angle \\(135^\\circ\\) is in the second quadrant. To find the reference angle, we subtract \\(135^\\circ\\) from \\(180^\\circ\\):\n   \\[\n   180^\\circ - 135^\\circ = 45^\\circ\n   \\]\n   So, the reference angle is \\(45^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Determine the cosine of the reference angle:**\n   The cosine of \\(45^\\circ\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\cos 45^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Consider the sign of cosine in the second quadrant:**\n   In the second quadrant, the cosine of an angle is negative. Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\cos 135^\\circ = -\\cos 45^\\circ = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\cos 135^\\circ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}\n\\]",
